  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mother School Society</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mothers School Society (MSS) has been working on women&#x2019;s economic empowerment and valuing women&#x2019;s work for the past 13 years. Almost 10 years ago, MSS began targeting and working with Palestinian women working in Israeli settlements. They provided women with awareness raising and mental health sessions to enhance their awareness of the violations of their rights  due to experiencing harshworking conditions. Women working in Israeli settlements are under a lot of pressure to provide for their families since the majority are women-headed households. Palestinian women workers in  Israeli settlements endure the most extreme human rights violations inthe workplace. The majority of women workers reside in areas near the settlements, unsupervised by the Palestinian Authority (PA), who cannot protect their labor rights.  Due to  social stigma (since Israeli settlements are regarded as illegal under internationalhumanitarian law (IHL) and international human rights law (IHRL)), these women are not encouraged to express their feelings and thedaily challenges and obstacles they are facing . Therefore, MSS works on continuing to empower women mentally and psychologically and builds their capacities to lead small business, providing them with alternative income generation activities that would support them to stop working in the settlements. MSS was able to support and mobilizing funding for 24 income generating projects/small businesses. As a result, women reported being more confident and engaged in public life/in their local communities. Coordinate  the development of the interviews/needs assessment forms (3 volunteers from MSS staff)  with the researcher.
Hold 3-5 Introductory meetings with potential stakeholders, CBOs, local councils.
Conduct interviews with women workers in Israeli settlements and conduct 2 focus group discussions and 10-15 individual interviews.
Conduct a round table as a closing event / to discuss the needs assessment findings and statistics
Share final reports
Conduct mental health and psychosocial support sessions</narrative>
  </description>
